lisa-design:
- Provider identity for SSOGroupMapping rows = SSOProviderConfig.Name (fallback to the config map key when Name is empty). This is the same string the login callback and SSOUserLink.Provider use (sso.Service keys providers by .Name), so provisioning and login reconcile match. Do NOT switch to the map key.
- Config provisioning (ProvisionSSOGroupMappings) is upsert-only: it creates referenced native groups and creates/updates (provider, externalGroup) mappings, but NEVER deletes mappings. This is deliberate so config-declared and admin-API-added mappings for the same provider coexist; "match config" was read as additive, not destructive.
- ReconcileSSOGroupMemberships only ever reads/writes source=sso rows. New sso memberships are inserted with ON CONFLICT(user_id,group_id) DO NOTHING so a pre-existing source=manual membership for the same group is never flipped to sso. De-provision deletes only source=sso rows. This is the core invariant: the IdP owns sso memberships, the admin owns manual ones, and neither clobbers the other.
- pip.go resolver is now native-only (ccf_user_groups). builtin.go's RequiredAdminGroups check still reads the raw SSO link groups directly — that is the admin BOOTSTRAP path (grant admin from an IdP group before any native group exists) and is intentionally OUT OF SCOPE for BCH-1331. Do not "fix" builtin.go to be native-only.
- RemoveMember: a missing membership still returns 204 (preserves the prior idempotent behaviour); a source=sso membership returns 403; only source=manual is deletable.
- DeleteGroup: 409 guard (memberCount>0) added BEFORE the existing cascade transaction. An empty group still cascades its SSO mappings then soft-deletes. The cascade no longer silently revokes memberships.
- Login reconcile is wired once in Callback() after findOrCreateUser succeeds (not inside each find/link/create path) and is best-effort: a reconcile error is logged and login proceeds. Startup provisioning in NewSSOHandler is likewise best-effort (logged, non-fatal).
- Source column: added via the gorm `default:manual` tag on UserGroupMembership; AutoMigrate already covers the table in both internal/service/migrator.go and internal/tests/migrate.go, so existing rows backfill to 'manual'. No new table, no new registration.
